 The cow herd, split out of World on 2026-09-03.

 IT CITES `Trees`, AND THAT IS A REAL DEPENDENCY RATHER THAN A LEFTOVER. The
 bull stands `bull-tree-gap` outside the tree line, so `bull-of` measures from
 `tree-road-offset`; the herd is placed relative to the conifers on purpose.
 The split made that edge visible instead of removing it.

 We say:

Section: The Cow Herd

 The boring CONSTANT on every segment, near the start and on the left: a bull
 leading ten cows and four calves in a deterministic jittered grid. No randomness
 anywhere -- the jitter is a sine of the index.


  bull-cp : Integer
  bull-cp = 128002

  cow-cp : Integer
  cow-cp = 128004

  cow-height : Real
  cow-height = 1.4

  calf-height : Real
  calf-height = cow-height / 2.0

  bull-height : Real
  bull-height = cow-height * 1.15

  bull-dist : Real
  bull-dist = 24.0

  bull-tree-gap : Real
  bull-tree-gap = 0.5

  herd-gap-behind-bull : Real
  herd-gap-behind-bull = 6.0

  herd-col-spacing : Real
  herd-col-spacing = 6.0

  herd-row-stagger : Real
  herd-row-stagger = 2.0

  herd-row-depth : Real
  herd-row-depth = 5.0

  herd-jitter-along : Real
  herd-jitter-along = 1.5

  herd-jitter-across : Real
  herd-jitter-across = 1.2

 The bull is authored per segment in the route table, like the cat and the pigs,
 so the whole schedule of surprises reads in one place.


  bull-of : Boolean -> List Critter
  bull-of (bull) =
    if bull then [Critter { along = bull-dist, across = 0.0 - (lane-width / 2.0 + tree-road-offset + bull-height / 2.0 + bull-tree-gap), codepoint = bull-cp, height = bull-height, face-right = False }]
    else []

  cows-from : Integer -> List Critter
  cows-from (i) =
    if i >= 14 then []
    else [cow-at i] & cows-from (i + 1)

  cow-at : Integer -> Critter
  cow-at (i) =
    let fi = real-from-int i
    in let col = real-from-int (i / 3)
    in let row = real-from-int (i - ((i / 3) * 3))
    in let along = bull-dist + herd-gap-behind-bull + col * herd-col-spacing + (row - 1.0) * herd-row-stagger + herd-jitter-along * r-sin (fi * 2.7)
    in let across = 0.0 - (lane-width / 2.0 + herd-road-offset + row * herd-row-depth + herd-jitter-across * r-cos (fi * 1.9))
    in Critter { along = along, across = across, codepoint = cow-cp, height = if i - ((i / 4) * 4) == 1 then calf-height else cow-height, face-right = True }

  fill-cows : Boolean -> List Critter
  fill-cows (bull) = (bull-of bull) & cows-from 0
